mbiguated_id":"G0284 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H5992G","headword":"Ἀμιναδάβ","transliteration":"Aminadab","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Amminadab","definition_en":"Ἀμιναδάβ, ὁ indecl. (Heb עַמִּינָדָב), \n Amminadab: Mat.1:4, Luk.3:33 (WH om.).†\n (AS)","source_line":387}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Aminadabe","count":3}]},"G3101":{"id":"G3101","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3101","disambiguated_id":"G3101 =","unique_id":"G3101","headword":"μαθητής","transliteration":"mathētēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"disciple","definition_en":"μαθητής, -οῦ, ὁ (μανθάνω), \n [in LXX only as seel. (A) in Jer.13:21 20:11 26(46):9 * ;] \na disciple: opposite to διδάσκαλος, Mat.10:24, Luk.6:40; Ἰωάννου, Mat.9:14, Luk.7:18, Jhn.3:25; τ. Φαρισσίων, Mat.22:16, Mrk.2:18, Luk.5:33; Μωυσέως, Jhn.9:28; Ἰησοῦ, Luk.6:17 7:11 19:37, Jhn.6:66 7:3 19:38; esp. the twelve, Mat.10:1 11:1, Mrk.7:17, Luk.8:9, Jo 2:2, al.; later, of Christians generally, Act.6:1, 2 7 9:19, al.; τ. κυρίου, Act.9:1.\n (AS)","source_line":3303}],"occurrence_count":262,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"discípulos","count":235},{"gloss":"discípulo","count":27}]},"G3122":{"id":"G3122","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3122","disambiguated_id":"G3122 =","unique_id":"G3122","headword":"μάλιστα","transliteration":"malista","lexical_morphology":"G:ADV","gloss_en":"especially","definition_en":"μάλιστα, see: μάλα.\n μάλα \n adv., [in LXX for אֲבָל, 3Ki.1:43, Dan LXX 10:21, al.; compar. for מ, Num.13:32 (31), al.; μᾶλλον ἠ (מ), Gen.19:9, al.; superlat., 2Ma.8:7, 4Ma.4:22 12:9 15:4 ;] \n__I. Pos., very, very much, exceedingly (cl.; LXX ut supr.; in NT its place is taken by λίαν, σφόδρα, etc.). \n __II. Compar., μᾶλλον. \n __1. Of increase, more; with qualifying words: πολλῷ, Mrk.10:48, Luk.18:39, Rom.5:15, 17, Php.2:12, al.; πόσῳ, Luk.12:24, Rom.11:12, al.; τοσούτῳ . . . ὅσῳ, Heb.10:25. \n __2. Of comparison, the more: Luk.5:15, Jhn.5:18, Act.5:14, 1Th.4:1, 10, 2Pe.1:10; ἔτι μ. καὶ μ., Php.1:9; with compar., Mrk.7:36, 2Co.7:13; πολλῴ μ. κρεῖσον, Php.1:23; μ. διαφέρειν, with genitive, Mat.6:26; μ. ἤ, Mat.18:13; with genitive, 1Co.14:18; as periphr. for compar., Act.20:35, 1Co.9:15, Gal.4:27; μ. δέ (EV, yea rather), Rom.8:34. \n __3. Of preference, rather, the rather, sooner: with qualifying words, πολλῷ, Mat.6:30, al.; πολύ, Heb.12:25; πόσῳ, Mat.7:11, al.; in a question, οὐ μ., 1Co.9:12; after a neg., Mat.10:6, al.; θέλω (εὐδοκῶ) μ., 1Co.14:5, 2Co.5:8; ζηλῶ, 1Co.14:1; with subst., τ. σκότος ἢ τ. φῶς, Jhn.3:19; μ. δέ, Gal.4:9. \n __III. Superl., μάλιστα\n, most, most of all, above all: Act.20:38 25:26, Gal.6:10, Php.4:22, 1Ti.4:10 5:8, 17, 2Ti.4:13, Tit.1:10, Phm 16, 2Pe.2:10; μ. γνώστης, Act.26:3 \n (AS)","source_line":3324}],"occurrence_count":12,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"principalmente","count":9},{"gloss":"especialmente","count":3}]},"G3429":{"id":"G3429","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3429","disambiguated_id":"G3429 =","unique_id":"G3429","headword":"μοιχάω","transliteration":"moichaō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to commit adultery","definition_en":"μοιχάω, -ῶ \n (= cl. μοιχεύω), [in LXX (mid., absol. and with accusative, with party of either sex as subj.) : Jer.3:8 5:7 7:9 9:2 23:14 29:23, Eze.16:32 23:37, 43 (נָאַף) * ;] \nto commit adultery with: with accusative, fem. In NT always mid, in same sense; of the man : absol., Mat.5:32 19:9 (WH, txt., R, mg., om.); before ἐπ᾽ αὐτήν, Mrk.10:11; of the woman: Mrk.10:12.†\n (AS)","source_line":3542}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"adultera","count":5}]},"G4054":{"id":"G4054","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4054","disambiguated_id":"G4054 = a Form of","unique_id":"G4055","headword":"περισσότερον","transliteration":"perissoteron","lexical_morphology":"G:ADV","gloss_en":"more excessive","definition_en":"περισσότερον, -ως, see: περισσῶς.\n περισσῶς\n adv. (περισσός) [in LXX: Psa.3